course: dictionary
lesson: 9887
title: Tailless: no tail
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tailless means having no tail. Look at the word: tail plus -less, and the ending -less means without. Hairless, careless and penniless follow the same pattern.
explain: «The great apes are four kinds of big, tailless, very clever animals: chimpanzees and bonobos, gorillas, and orangutans, and every one of them is endangered.» The words big and clever are about the animals' bodies and minds, so tailless is a description too. It tells you what the apes are like.
explain: The word can also describe machines. An aircraft or kite built without a tail is tailless as well. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: a tailless frog is a frog with no tail. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Tailless means having no tail.
fact: The ending -less means without, so tail plus -less means without a tail.
fact: Adult frogs are tailless, but tadpoles have tails.
fact: Great apes, such as gorillas and orangutans, are tailless.
fact: Tailless can also describe an aircraft or kite built without a tail, and some lizards are tailless for a while after they lose their tail.
exercise: «The great apes are four kinds of big, tailless, very clever animals.» What does tailless mean? | Having a tail that can grab branches | *Having no tail | Having a bright, fluffy tail | Having a very long, curly tail
exercise: Which animal is tailless as an adult? | *An adult frog | A tadpole | A squirrel with a bushy tail | A monkey with a long tail
exercise: Tailless is made from tail and -less. What does -less mean? | *Without | Very | Full of | Again
test: «The lizard lost its tail in the fight and was tailless for a while.» What does tailless mean here? | Having a new tail | *Having no tail | Hiding in the grass | Running very fast
test: Which word has the same -less pattern as tailless? | *Hairless | Careful | Tailor | Hairy
exam: A kite described as tailless is one that | Has the longest tail of all | Can only fly at night | *Is built without a tail | Has lost its string
